====================================================================================================
PART A   AUDIT of w7_pl_hess.py:  its 'Hessian' is H_ab = Re tr(lam_a lam_b M), the
         UNSYMMETRISED second derivative D_aD_b of Re tr(U M) at U = e.  The Levi-Civita
         Hessian in the left-invariant frame is  Hess F = (1/2)(D_vD_w + D_wD_v)F  because
         grad^{LC}_{lam_a} lam_b = (1/2)[lam_a, lam_b]  (the frame is not holonomic).
         For SU(2):  lam_b lam_a + lam_a lam_b = -(lam_a.lam_b)/2 * 1
            => Hess Re tr(UM) = -(1/4)Re tr(UM) * 1 = -(1/2) cos(th_{UM}) * 1
            => Hess S_p       = +(beta/4) cos(th_{UM}) * 1      (SCALAR, |.| <= beta/4)
         so  sup(-lambda_min H) = 1/2 for SU(2) exactly (attained at M = 1).
====================================================================================================
